\begin_layout Standard
Reinforcement learning (RL) is a subfield of Machine Learning which illustrates
 a scenario where an agent interacts with an environment and has to learn
 a strategy from a (delayed) reward.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
xx It is espedially suitable for problems such as games or control strategies,
 where the solution is somewhat obvious, but the strategy how to achieve
 it is not clear.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
RL thus enables the search for new solution strategies that are free of
 human bias and can reveal new solution paths in many areas.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To do so, the agent receives the current state (observations) of the environment
 and can decide on an action, thus reaching a subsequent state and a reward.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The environment is formalized as Markov Decision Process (MDP), which are
 a stochastic form of determinism so that in each state, when performing
 an action, the same subsequent state is reached with a certain probability.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Learning a policy relies on trial and error, with the agent having to carefully
 weigh up exploration and exploitation to cope with the limited resources
 an agent has at his disposal.
\end_layout

