\begin_layout Paragraph
Imlementation
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:depth-based-gp-implementation"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Fixed nodes can be determined root-down for a real subset of nodes of the
 origin tree and are unaffected by the evolution process.
 In order to continue to use classical GP evolution with the same intuition,
 some procedures, especially when generating random trees, must therefore
 be adapted.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The fixed core of a tree must be contiguous in this implementation, but
 can offer starting points for evolutions at any number of points at different
 heights.
 The node depth, which normally indicates the distance to the tree root,
 thus almost completely loses its meaning for the GP process.
 The depth of a node is therefore replaced with a shell-based interpretation,
 in which the distance of a node to the next fixed node is used as.
 Due to the high branching factor in trees with several GP interfaces, however,
 the layer model also loses its function, which is why the number of nodes
 replaces the tree depth as a complexity limit and complexity target in
 random tree generation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Nodesize-based build options including the full- and grow-method.
 Randomly generated trees should cover the entire search space and have
 the structuring Full/Grow options to have the same properties of non-fixed
 generated trees.
\end_layout

