\begin_layout Paragraph
Implementation 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
While simplifying formulas for more efficient evaluation can be done easily,
 creating a simpler branch is a much more complex problem.
 The extracted expression is simplified using symbolic mathematics, for
 which the Python library SymPy 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "10.7717/peerj-cs.103"

\end_inset

 was extended.
 The simplified expression is then evaluated as an abstract ayntax tree
 (AST), which can be transformed into a GP tree by recursively pattern matching
 the components to the available GP operators.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Due to its complexity, this process can lead to many special cases and in
 any case requires extensive adaptations, for example to avoid arity-changing
 or unwanted transformations as in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:sympy-custom-gp-operators"

\end_inset

 or to handle special cases of solutions, as can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:sympy-sonderfälle"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this work, the effects of simplified expert heuristics were not further
 processed, as this would have required a reinterpretation and weighting
 of various changes.
 Thus, the benefits of unified formulas could not be evaluated either.
 This approach was only used to improve the performance of the existing
 approach by trying to simplify Pareto entries.
\end_layout

