\begin_layout Paragraph
Domain Expert solutions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following, three solution strategies are examined more closely by
 experts as origin.
 A simple one, which relies on maximum acceleration, is compared with two
 extensive ones as a short solution.
 One of them is a formula based on parabolas, the other is an extremely
 improved, nested if-statement that treats the reversal points as special
 cases.
 At sensible points, the options of fixed core structure and obligatory
 acceleration were tested.
 Since action 1 cannot be selected for the latter option, the regression
 error cannot drop to 0 (0.023 for Sarsa-200, 0.066 for Sarsa-75).
 
\end_layout

